WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.436
-Our next guest is an Emmy
nominated comedian and actress

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.504
you know, from her work
on "Saturday Night Live"

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:07.774
and movies such as
"Trainwreck in Ibiza."

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.509
Her new series,
"I Love That For You,"

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.111
begins streaming
April 29th and premieres

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.380
May 1st on Showtime.
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:19.385
-My dream was always
to be a host on SVN.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:22.689
-What is that?
-The Special Value Network, duh.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.392
I don't know. I was just
thinking, what if I did it?

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.027
What if I, like, auditioned?

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:31.431
I mean, of course
I would not do anything

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.166
that would take me
away from Cleveland

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:37.070
without discussing it
with you first, but...

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.439
-Sorry. I'm confused.
We've been on, like, two dates.

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.909
-Hmm, three. [ Chuckles ]

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.677
-Are you counting our run-in
at Walgreens?

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.913
-The point is, I think we were
both feeling like this

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:50.783
was kind of it for us.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:54.687
We kissed on our first date.
What was that about?

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.923
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.491
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.494
our very good friend,
Vanessa Bayer.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:04.497
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:11.170 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:17.844 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.611
-Oh, wow.
-Now, Vanessa?

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.347
-Yes?
I'm so happy to see you

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.415
in person again.
-Oh, my God.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.284
-I feel like it's not
just been forever

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.851
since you've been on the show,
I bet it's been a long time

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:28.054
since you've even been
on the East Coast.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.855
-You're absolutely right.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.926
-Yeah, it's --
-I did my research, you know.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.326
-Well, because, you know,
I live in L.A. now.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:36.495
You know, I'm an L.A. girl,
I guess now.

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.464
-Everyone said that about you.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:39.666
-Even when you were on "SNL,"
we were like,

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.200
"She's supposed to be
an L.A. girl."

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.268
-"She's so L.A."
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.103
I have a car,
which is incredible.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.940
-Amazing. Congrats.
-Thank you so much. It's been...

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.542
It's like a big purse.
You can put so much stuff in it.

00:01:50.542 --> 00:01:53.212
-Yeah, that's a really nice way
of describing it.

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.715
So was it hard here in sort of
little purse New York?

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.883
-[ Laughing ] Yeah, yeah.
That's why I always say.

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:00.620
I say, "That's a little purse
New York."

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.887
-And I love it, but --
-The Big Apple.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:04.156
More like the little purse.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.726
That's what I say. [ Laughs ]

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.960
But no, I love it.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.663
And, you know, I hop in my car.
It's a Tesla.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.266
Isn't that a big deal, you guys?
I don't want to be, like...

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.134
bragging about it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.602
-Well, I don't even know
what reaction you want.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.304
It's -- Yeah, well.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.173
I guess I got applause.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.641
And it's great because
it drives me,

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.243
because I'm not
"great at driving,"

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:26.079
but I can drive up and see Gwen.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.214
-Yeah, your friend Gwen.
-My friend Gwen.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.216
-Now, I should say this.
You've said this like this --

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.151
and don't take this
the wrong way.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.919
-[ Laughs ] Okay.
-You have --

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:36.322
a lot of people would, like,
come to "SNL," on the cast,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.356
and they'd be like,
"This is my friend from home,

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:38.524
this is my friend from home."

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.626
You only ever had one friend,
and it was Gwen.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.995
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:45.698
Like, everybody knows Gwen.
Everybody loves Gwen.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.999
-Yeah, everybody loves Gwen.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:48.134
Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.835
I mean, I have more than one
friend.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:52.105
-But you just only brought Gwen.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:55.174
Gwen and my brother Jonah,
those are the two staples

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.475
that I always had with me.

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:57.910
-It was -- we all -- the rest of
the cast, we always said,

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.578
"The nice thing about Vanessa
is there's not a lot

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:00.847
of names to learn."

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:04.417
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.185
How is Gwen?
-Gwen is great.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.553
Gwen just had her second baby.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.655
-Oh, congratulations.
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.958
-And how is Jonah?
-Jonah is great. He's married.

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:15.027
He's going back to school

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.762
to become a mental health
counselor.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:19.364
-Okay, good for him.
-So, yeah, I guess.

00:03:19.364 --> 00:03:20.867
That's my brother.
He's very smart.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.302
-That's awesome.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.036
-So happy to hear all of that.
-Yes. Yeah.

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:25.471
-And so you're back
in New York City,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.805
and you have this
wonderful show.

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:29.375
Now, this show pulls
from two things about your life

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.476
that are true.
-Yes.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.011
-When you were young,
you had leukemia.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.946
-Yes.
-And when you had it,

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.281
you fell in love with QVC.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.783
This was a true love you had.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.419
-When I was little,
I used to love QVC so much,

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.686
I would tape it.

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:44.623
I would just -- I just loved
the way the hosts talked

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:47.627
about products and the way
that they measured them

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.629
and they just, you know -- you
know, they would say, like --

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:52.331
you know, I was like a little
kid, but they'd be like,

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.333
"This is perfect out for
a brunch with the ladies

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.901
or your daughter's graduation."

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.504
I'd be like, "I could take this
to my daughter's graduation."

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.039
Like, I was nine.

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.574
I didn't have a daughter, but
it just -- like, I just loved,

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:04.276
like, the stories they would
tell about the products

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.879
and stuff, and I just was
completely mesmerized by it.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.282
-Well, one thing I genuinely
love about this show

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:12.985
is the first episode's so
wonderful, and it does speak to

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:15.822
that being a specific skill,
like the selling of

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.157
these products and not just
the product itself,

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.026
but putting that story
on top of it.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.660
-Right, right, right, right.
Yes.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.696
-And so in the show,
Molly Shannon plays

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.265
sort of your mentee,
I guess you would say.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.833
Your mentor.
You're the mentee.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.368
-I'm the mentee, yeah.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.770
I mean, you know,
Molly is the best.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.773
I met her at
the "SNL" 40th anniversary.

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:37.643
I think I asked Shoemaker to,
like, introduce us.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.378
I was too scared to...
-Yeah.

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.747
-Now knowing her,
she would have been nice

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:42.982
even if I had gone up myself.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.118
But anyway, yeah, she was --
-Sort of famously

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.053
the nicest person ever, yeah.
-The famously nicest person

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.721
ever.
We're both from Cleveland.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.656
Like, we both love
all the same places.

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:53.059
My favorite restaurant in
Cleveland is this place,

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.761
Tommy's, that I always shout-out
so they'll send me gift cards.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.764
[ Laughter ]
But she... [ Laughs ]

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:03.202
-Your Tesla has a stack of
Tommy's gift cards.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.505
-And, look, I don't expect
a free Tesla...

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:07.707
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:11.243
But... [ Laughs ]
I love free stuff.

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:12.678
What can I say?

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:17.316
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.518
But Molly used to work
at Tommy's,

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:21.220
and she knows Tommy.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.989
And again, I don't know.
Throw me a couple.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:27.159
But um...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:29.028
Yeah, so we have, like,
a lot of -- you know,

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:31.564
we're from the same exact
suburbs of Cleveland.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.033
And so it's really fun to talk
to her about that stuff,

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.502
but she's also just such
an incredible --

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.570
she's just the best.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.438
She's the best on screen
and off screen.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:42.375
And it was really fun because
she wasn't as familiar

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.544
with home shopping, and so
I sort of -- even though --

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:47.613
I know, right? What?

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:51.583
And so even like though she's
like my mentor in the show,

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:53.319
when we would be, like,
rehearsing and stuff,

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.753
I'd be like, "Molly,
you have to like touch

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:56.822
all of the products.
You have to, like, show --

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:59.058
you have to, like,
run your fingernail under them.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.692
You have to wear 5,000 rings

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:02.095
because they always have so much
jewelry on."

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:04.130
Like, I kind of showed her
the ropes.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.798
And she, of course, is like...

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.133
You know, she learns fast
because she's...

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.134
-She's Molly Shannon.

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:10.203
-She's Molly Shannon.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.505
-I have a lot more
to ask about this.

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:14.640
In particular, I want to ask
about the similarities between

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.644
QVC and "SNL," not just
the three-initial thing.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.381
We'll be right back with more
from Vanessa Bayer.

